1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,099
X-rays are invisible, high-energy light that passes through your body.

2
00:00:05,099 --> 00:00:09,099
Along the way, your cells absorb some of that energy.

3
00:00:09,099 --> 00:00:13,939
It knocks electrons loose, making free radicals that attack DNA.

4
00:00:13,939 --> 00:00:16,140
Both strands can snap.

5
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:19,980
If the repair goes wrong, a mutation is left behind.

6
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:24,859
That cell may start dividing out of control, the first step toward cancer.

7
00:00:24,859 --> 00:00:29,460
The risk from one scan is tiny, so doctors use the lowest dose possible.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
That cell may start dividing out of control, so doctors use the lowest dose possible.
